/**
 * @defgroup Foundation_Utils Utils
 * @ingroup Foundation
 * @brief Low-level move, swap, and utility helpers.
 *
 * Utils provides the small operations needed by Foundation containers without
 * requiring `<utility>`. The current public surface consists of Move and Swap.
 * Empty historical placeholders such as `Forward.h` and `Exchange.h` are not
 * installed and are not part of the supported API.
 *
 * @section FoundationUtilsHeaders Public Headers
 *
 * | Need | Header |
 * | ---- | ------ |
 * | Entire Foundation library | `#include <Foundation.h>` |
 * | Entire Utils module | `#include <Foundation_Utils.h>` |
 * | Nested module umbrella | `#include <Foundation/Utils.h>` |
 * | Move only | `#include <Foundation/Utils/Move.h>` |
 * | Swap only | `#include <Foundation/Utils/Swap.h>` |
 *
 * @section FoundationUtilsUsage Basic Usage
 *
 * @code{.cpp}
 * int first = 3;
 * int second = 9;
 * Foundation::Utils::Swap(first, second);
 *
 * MoveOnly destination(Foundation::Utils::Move(source));
 * @endcode
 *
 * Move performs an rvalue cast; it does not move data by itself. The selected
 * constructor or assignment operator defines the resulting transfer and the
 * valid state of the moved-from object. Swap requires move construction and
 * move assignment compatible with the supplied type. Move itself is
 * `constexpr` and `noexcept`; Swap does not promise `noexcept` because the
 * selected type's move operations may throw.
 *
 * @section FoundationUtilsExample Runnable Example
 *
 * `Foundation_Utils_MoveAndSwap` demonstrates swapping integers and moving a
 * non-copyable object. See @ref Foundation_Examples "Examples" for build and
 * launch instructions.
 */

/**
 * @namespace Foundation::Utils
 * @ingroup Foundation_Utils
 * @brief Low-level move and swap helpers.
 */
